statement:
Two pthread workers each execute the following once. The shared counter starts at 0. All accesses to counter use the same initialized mutex; assume no errors and that main joins both threads.

```c
pthread_mutex_lock(&mu);
int local = counter;
pthread_mutex_unlock(&mu);
local += 1;
pthread_mutex_lock(&mu);
counter = local;
pthread_mutex_unlock(&mu);
```

Which set contains exactly the possible final values of counter?
